 "notes": "Headline result: new SN1987A gamma-ray decay bound on the ALP-photon coupling (Section 4, red \"SN1987A (This work)\" closed excluded region in Fig.3), from non-observation of a gamma-ray burst by SMM after SN1987A neutrinos, including photon-coalescence production extending the reach to m_a ~ 280-295 MeV. No ancillary data file shipped; figure is a raster PNG (combinedBoundsPlot.png). Boundary extracted by pixel analysis: log axes calibrated from decade ticks (m in MeV converted to eV via x1e6; g already in GeV^-1). Closed lens traced as lower boundary (left->right, the newly excluded reach) then upper boundary (right->left, flat ~8e-11 = the yellow diffuse-flux line where red meets already-excluded regions). Region spans m_a ~ 0.032-295 MeV, minimum coupling ~1.5e-12 GeV^-1 near 130-170 MeV. Paper quotes 3sigma (F_gamma<1.78 cm^-1) as the primary bright-red bound and 2sigma (F_gamma<1.19 cm^-1) as a slightly larger darker-red region; traced outer boundary corresponds to ~2sigma, reported at confidence_level 0.95. Bound is not dark-matter-density dependent (SN source), so dm_density null.",
